 /*
- * SWEET SE7 FIFO I2C / GT9896 Yellowstone / Focaltech 54:52 bring-up.
- * Call once after the scheduler is running; all work runs on one thread.
- * Requires ABL-loaded GENI I2C firmware; votes L11C through sweet_rpmh.c.
- * No firmware/config upload or direct PMIC writes. Only IC data write:
- * zero to GT9896's event status after reading a report. See touch2/report.md.
+ * Motorola Moto G05 (MT6768 "lamu") touch screen: ILITEK TDDI on SPI2.
+ *
+ * Linux (Android) has initialised the IC, loaded its firmware and left the
+ * MediaTek SPI controller (spi2 @ 0x11012000) configured for it; the hand-off
+ * module keeps the controller's runtime-PM "on" so its clocks are still
+ * running. This driver only polls the IC's report register:
+ *
+ *   tx: 0x83 0 0 ...            (SPI_READ)
+ *   rx: [0] ?  [1] 0xa3 (ACK)  [2] ?  [3...] report packet
+ *
+ * Report packets (ilitek_v3 driver, oem/touchscreen/ILITEK9883C):
+ *   0x5a  43 bytes, 10 fingers * 4 bytes from byte 1: x = (b1 & 0xf0) << 4 | b2,
+ *         y = (b1 & 0x0f) << 8 | b3, both 0..2047; ff ff ff = no finger.
+ *   0x5b  72 bytes, 10 fingers * 5 bytes from byte 1: 16-bit x, 16-bit y.
+ * The last byte is a checksum: (-sum of the others) & 0xff.
+ *
+ * The transfer uses the controller's DMA from two static cache-line aligned
+ * buffers (the controller has 36-bit DMA addresses). All reads are logged
+ * rate-limited so the first run on the phone shows what the IC really sends.
  */
